thentication flow, payment processing), call them out explicitly.",
  |       "task_prompt": "<context>\nThe team is auditing a Node.js Express microservice before the v2.2 release. The service handles authentication and payment processing with real transactions and PII storage. Your reconnaissance establishes the foundation for security, performance, and integration analysis.\n</context>\n\n<assignment>\nDiscover and map the complete structure of the /src directory:\n\n1. Start with directory enumeration to understand the layout\n2. Locate the main entry point (typically server.js, app.js, or index.js)\n3. Trace route registration — find where Express routes are defined and mounted\n4. Identify all route handlers, grouping them by functional domain\n5. Map the middleware chain — what runs before handlers execute?\n6. Discover data layer components — database clients, query builders, models\n7. Find external integration points — payment APIs, auth providers, third-party services\n8. Note any configuration files, environment variable usage, or secrets management\n\nUse grep to discover patterns, then file_read to understand what you found. For authentication and payment routes, trace the full execution path from route registration through middleware to handler to data layer.\n\nProduce a structured inventory with file paths and descriptions. Organize findings so downstream agents can quickly locate:\n- Attack surface areas (SecurityAuditor needs all input boundaries)\n- Database interaction points (PerformanceAnalyst needs query locations)\n- Module boundaries and data flows (IntegrationReviewer needs integration points)\n\nThis is exploratory work in an unknown codebase. Discover using your tools rather than assuming structure.\n</assignment>",
