  | ### Vulnerability: Missing Input Validation on Financial Parameters
  | **Location:** src/payments/checkout.js:8-9  
  | **Severity:** HIGH  
  | **Evidence:** No validation of amount or orderId parameters:
  | ```javascript
  | const { orderId, amount } = req.body;
  | const userId = req.user.userId;
  | ```
  | **Attack Vector:**
  | - `amount` could be negative, allowing users to add balance instead of deducting
  | - `amount` could be a string, object, or null causing type coercion issues
  | - `orderId` could be an object leading to SQL injection or type confusion
  | - No validation that the order exists or belongs to the user
  | - No maximum amount check to prevent large fraudulent transactions
  | 
  | **Remediation:** Add comprehensive input validation:
  | ```javascript
  | const { orderId, amount } = req.body;
  | 
  | // Validate amount
  | if (typeof amount !== 'number' || !Number.isFinite(amount)) {
  |   return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid amount: must be a number' });
  | }
  | if (amount <= 0) {
  |   return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid amount: must be positive' });
  | }
  | if (amount > 1000000) { // Set reasonable maximum
  |   return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Amount exceeds maximum allowed' });
  | }
  | 
  | // Validate orderId
  | if (typeof orderId !== 'string' || !/^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/.test(orderId)) {
  |   return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid orderId format' });
  | }
  | 
  | // Verify order exists and belongs to user
  | const order = await db.getOrder(orderId);
  | if (!order || order.user_id !== req.user.userId) {
  |   return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Order not found or unauthorized' });
  | }
  | ```
  | 
