  | ### Vulnerability: Missing Input Validation on Transaction ID
  | **Location:** src/payments/refund.js:8  
  | **Severity:** HIGH  
  | **Evidence:** No validation of transactionId parameter:
  | ```javascript
  | const { transactionId } = req.body;
  | ```
  | **Attack Vector:**
  | - `transactionId` could be an object, array, or malicious string
  | - Enables SQL injection attempts if query construction changes
  | - Could cause application crashes or unexpected behavior
  | - Facilitates transaction ID enumeration attacks
  | 
  | **Remediation:** Add input validation:
  | ```javascript
  | const { transactionId } = req.body;
  | 
  | if (!transactionId || typeof transactionId !== 'number') {
  |   return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid transactionId: must be a number' });
  | }
  | 
  | if (!Number.isInteger(transactionId) || transactionId <= 0) {
  |   return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid transactionId: must be a positive integer' });
  | }
  | ```
