  | ### Vulnerability: Weak JWT Secret Configuration
  | **Location:** .env.example:9, src/auth/login.js:34, src/auth/middleware.js:12,33  
  | **Severity:** HIGH  
  | **Evidence:** Example file shows weak secret, no validation that production secret is strong:
  | ```javascript
  | // .env.example
  | JWT_SECRET=your-secret-here
  | 
  | // No validation in code that JWT_SECRET is set or strong
  | return jwt.sign({ userId }, process.env.JWT_SECRET, { expiresIn: '24h' });
  | ```
  | **Attack Vector:**
  | - If developers use the example secret in production, attackers can forge tokens
  | - No minimum entropy requirement for JWT_SECRET
  | - No startup validation that JWT_SECRET is configured
  | - Forged tokens allow complete authentication bypass
  | 
  | **Remediation:** Add secret validation on startup:
  | ```javascript
  | // In src/index.js or a config validation module
  | function validateConfig() {
  |   if (!process.env.JWT_SECRET) {
  |     throw new Error('JWT_SECRET environment variable is required');
  |   }
  |   
  |   if (process.env.JWT_SECRET.length < 32) {
  |     throw new Error('JWT_SECRET must be at least 32 characters');
  |   }
  |   
  |   if (process.env.JWT_SECRET === 'your-secret-here') {
  |     throw new Error('JWT_SECRET cannot be the default example value');
  |   }
  |   
  |   if (!process.env.DATABASE_URL) {
  |     throw new Error('DATABASE_URL environment variable is required');
  |   }
  | }
  | 
  | validateConfig();
  | ```
  | 
