  | ### Vulnerability: Missing Rate Limiting on Authentication Endpoint
  | **Location:** src/auth/login.js:6, src/index.js  
  | **Severity:** MODERATE  
  | **Evidence:** No rate limiting middleware on login endpoint:
  | ```javascript
  | router.post('/login', async (req, res) => {
  |   const { email, password } = req.body;
  |   // No rate limiting
  | ```
  | **Attack Vector:**
  | - Enables brute force attacks on user credentials
  | - No protection against credential stuffing attacks
  | - Can be used for user enumeration (timing differences between valid/invalid emails)
  | - Allows DoS by flooding login endpoint
  | 
  | **Remediation:** Implement rate limiting:
  | ```javascript
  | const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
  | 
  | const loginLimiter = rateLimit({
  |   windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  |   max: 5, // 5 attempts per window
  |   message: 'Too many login attempts, please try again later',
  |   standardHeaders: true,
  |   legacyHeaders: false,
  | });
  | 
  | router.post('/login', loginLimiter, async (req, res) => {
  |   // ... existing code
  | });
  | ```
