  | ### Vulnerability: Sensitive Error Information Disclosure
  | **Location:** src/auth/login.js:27-28, src/payments/checkout.js:37-38, src/payments/refund.js:30-31  
  | **Severity:** MODERATE  
  | **Evidence:** Detailed errors logged to console without sanitization:
  | ```javascript
  | console.error('Login error:', err);
  | console.error('Checkout error:', err);
  | console.error('Refund error:', err);
  | ```
  | **Attack Vector:**
  | - Error objects may contain sensitive data (SQL queries, user data, stack traces)
  | - Console logs may be aggregated to centralized logging systems without proper access controls
  | - Helps attackers understand internal system structure
  | - May leak PII in error messages
  | 
  | **Remediation:** Implement structured logging with sanitization:
  | ```javascript
  | const logger = require('./utils/logger'); // Implement proper logger
  | 
  | try {
  |   // ... existing code
  | } catch (err) {
  |   // Log sanitized error without sensitive data
  |   logger.error('Login failed', {
  |     error: err.message,
  |     code: err.code,
  |     // Do not log: err.stack, user input, SQL queries
  |   });
  |   return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
  | }
  | ```
