  | ### Vulnerability: Missing Security Headers
  | **Location:** src/index.js  
  | **Severity:** MODERATE  
  | **Evidence:** No helmet middleware for security headers:
  | ```javascript
  | app.use(cors());
  | app.use(bodyParser.json());
  | // Missing: app.use(helmet());
  | ```
  | **Attack Vector:**
  | - Missing Content-Security-Policy allows XSS attacks
  | - Missing X-Frame-Options allows clickjacking
  | - Missing Strict-Transport-Security allows MITM attacks
  | - Missing X-Content-Type-Options allows MIME sniffing attacks
  | 
  | **Remediation:** Add helmet middleware:
  | ```javascript
  | const helmet = require('helmet');
  | 
  | app.use(helmet({
  |   contentSecurityPolicy: {
  |     directives: {
  |       defaultSrc: ["'self'"],
  |       styleSrc: ["'self'", "'unsafe-inline'"],
  |     },
  |   },
  |   hsts: {
  |     maxAge: 31536000,
  |     includeSubDomains: true,
  |     preload: true
  |   },
  | }));
  | ```
  | 
  | ---
  | 
  | ### Vulnerability: Overly Permissive CORS Configuration
  | **Location:** src/index.js:12  
  | **Severity:** MODERATE  
  | **Evidence:** CORS enabled without origin restrictions:
  | ```javascript
  | app.use(cors());
  | ```
  | **Attack Vector:**
  | - Allows any origin to make authenticated requests to the API
  | - Enables CSRF attacks if cookies are used
  | - Allows malicious sites to make requests on behalf of authenticated users
  | - Violates principle of least privilege
  | 
  | **Remediation:** Configure CORS with specific origins:
  | ```javascript
  | const corsOptions = {
  |   origin: process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS?.split(',') || ['https://yourdomain.com'],
  |   credentials: true,
  |   optionsSuccessStatus: 200
  | };
  | 
  | app.use(cors(corsOptions));
  | ```
  | 
  | ---
  | 
  | ### Vulnerability: Missing Request Size Limits
  | **Location:** src/index.js:13  
  | **Severity:** MODERATE  
  | **Evidence:** No size limit on JSON body parser:
  | ```javascript
  | app.use(bodyParser.json());
  | ```
  | **Attack Vector:**
  | - Allows attackers to send extremely large JSON payloads
  | - Can exhaust server memory causing DoS
  | - Can fill up disk space if requests are logged
  | - No protection against JSON bomb attacks
  | 
  | **Remediation:** Add size limits:
  | ```javascript
  | app.use(bodyParser.json({ 
  |   limit: '10kb',
  |   strict: true 
  | }));
  | ```
  | 
